# prompt: bullet ricochet whine off stone
# tags: ricochet, bullet, whine, impact
# The whine is a Doppler shift, so it falls and it must start *after* the
# impact — the bullet is already leaving when you hear it. A sine rather than a
# saw for the sweep: a ricochet has almost no harmonics left by the time it
# reaches the listener, and a saw here reads as a cartoon.
sound "bullet ricochet" 520ms impact
  hit: noise white >> hp ~3000Hz[1500..7000] | gain 0.4 attack 0ms decay 30ms
  spark: modal metal ~5200Hz[2500..9000] Q120 | gain 0.16 decay 200ms
  whine: chirp sine ~3800Hz[2000..8000] -> ~900Hz[400..2000] in 380ms | gain 0.26 attack 5ms decay 420ms delay 15ms
  room: noise pink >> lp ~3000Hz[1200..6000] >> verb 220ms mix 0.4 | gain 0.1 decay 180ms delay 20ms
